lifeos-nix patch f-docintegrity-rename — finish the PAI→LIFEOS rename in the doc-integrity chain

PROBLEM
  Upstream 7.1.1 moved the config root (~/.claude → ~/.claude/LIFEOS) and renamed the system
  docs, but left the doc-integrity chain half-renamed. In hooks/handlers/DocCrossRefIntegrity.ts
  and hooks/lib/change-detection.ts, dead 'PAI/' string-gates and a mixed-case 'LifeOS/'
  ref-regex silently disable the checks: system-doc edits aren't detected (ARCHITECTURE_SUMMARY
  isn't auto-regenerated), doc cross-references aren't validated, and core-system doc
  categorization is dead. Verified against the pinned upstream tree — this is upstream's
  unfinished rename, not a local artifact.

FIX (2 files; mechanical + one structural)
  DocCrossRefIntegrity.ts: path-gates 'PAI/' → '/DOCUMENTATION/' (system docs live in
  LIFEOS/DOCUMENTATION/); ref-regex 'LifeOS/' → 'LIFEOS/' and 'config/PAI' → 'config/LIFEOS'
  (real refs are 'LIFEOS/DOCUMENTATION/X/Y.md'); drift reference label 'PAI/' → 'LIFEOS/'.
  change-detection.ts: HIGH_PRIORITY_PATHS + core-system regex use 7.1.1 doc names
  (PAISYSTEM→LifeosSystemArchitecture, THEHOOKSYSTEM→HookSystem, THEDELEGATION→DelegationSystem,
  MEMORYSYSTEM→MemorySystem); PHILOSOPHICAL /PAI\// → /LIFEOS\//. STRUCTURAL: the core-system
  match in categorizeChange() sat inside the `if (path.includes('skills/'))` block (5.0
  skills/PAI/ layout) — moved ABOVE it, since 7.1.1 core docs are in LIFEOS/DOCUMENTATION/,
  not skills/, and would otherwise fall through to generic 'documentation'.

SCOPE / CO-EXISTENCE
  Two hook files, disjoint from all other patches (f-telos, f-derived-watch, f4-*). Neither
  file is touched by any other patch. Cosmetic comment examples mentioning PAISECURITYSYSTEM
  left as-is (not functional).

VERIFICATION
  All 6 mapped core-system doc paths exist under LIFEOS/DOCUMENTATION/; actual refs verified as
  'LIFEOS/DOCUMENTATION/X/Y.md' (regex matches); both files parse (bun build). Hunks via diff -u.

